    <statement><p>Let <m>\mathbf a = \langle 5, 2 \rangle</m> and 
<m>\mathbf b = \langle 5, -3 \rangle</m>.</p>
<p>Show that there are scalars s and t so that
<m>s \mathbf a + t \mathbf b = \langle 0, -10 \rangle</m></p>
<p>You might want to sketch the vectors to get some intuition.</p>
<p><m>s =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>t =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
